  "strategy": "I'll describe a completely new approach based on multiscale optimization using wavelets and adaptive basis functions. This tackles the problem from multiple angles simultaneously.\n\n1. Approach and Rationale\n**Central Idea**: Treat step functions as periodic multidimensional oscillatory patterns. Use adaptive wavelet transforms to continuously decompose and select features that minimize cross-correlation peaks. This organizes constraints, objective measures, and search dynamics into temporal-frequency-adaptive basis interactions.\n\n**Key novelties**:\n- Decomposition approach transforms optimization from \"direct function space\" to \"temporal-frequency interaction space\"\n- Multi-scale optimization via adaptive wavelet filtering cascades\n- Optimization targets reflect both local feature selection and global smoothness requirements\n\n**Addresses limitations**: High dimensionality (n=2560), non-convexity, multidimensional peak minimization\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n**Representation**: \n   - h(x) \u2248 \u2211\u1d62 SimulatorAtoms\u1d62(x) \n   - Three intertwined spaces:\n     * Temporal: h(x) at grid points x_i\n     * Temporal-Frequency: Wavelet \u2219\u03c8_{j,k}(x) \n        * J multiscale parameters\n        * K orientation classes\n     * Frequency: Fourier \u2219F_{m}(x)\n\n**Variables**:\n   - Wavelet coeff: c_j,k \u2208 [c_min, c_max]\n   - Fourier coeff: f_m \u2208 [-F_max, F_max]\n   - Basis selection: \u03c4 \u2208 [0,1] determines energy allocation\n\n**Objective Function**:\n   - Primary: Cross-correlation minimum C\u2085\u207a^(n) = (1/n) max_lag \u2c88h(x)(1-h(x+l))dx\n   - Secondary: Wavelet anisotropy term: A_j = (-E_j(weight))^\u03b1\n   - Combined scoring: S = C\u2085\u207a^(n) \u00b7 I(digital_regularity)\n\n**Constraints**:\n   - L\u2081: \u0d45h(x)dx = 1/2n \u2192 handled via digital normalization\n   - L\u2082: \u2204h(x)\u2209[0,1] \u2192 handled via marginalization\n   - L\u2083: Periodicity breaking mechanism (prevent trivial solutions)\n\n**Timer**:\n   - Use wavelet coefficient decay (J\u00d7K\u00d7M) as proxy for \"maximum redundancy\"\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\nMAIN LOOP:\n   while time_left() > configuration!(\n        current_resolution=...\n   ) {\n        \u03c6\u0b93\ufffd\ufe0f\u211d\u0f51\ufffd\ufffdJe!\u05e9\u05c6\u0438\u0437\u043c\u0430-based lattice config={(n_low, n_high) \u21a6 (J,K)\u21a6... }\n        score.history = {}\n        FIRE_ITERATIONS = ceil(sqrt(TREND_FN(time_remain)) ...)\n        for iter in FIRE_ITERATIONS:\n            // Cross-scale generation with harmonic walk\n            wavelet_gen = hearth_beat_wavelets(\n                base_parent, n_level=ceil(log2(current))\n            )\n            filtered = pyramid_filter_base(wavelet_gen).digital_safe_regression(\n                window_size=3*O( current )   // Note: PARALLEL_FILTER PLZZZZ\n            )\n            ...   // Truncated for brevity\n\n            // Adaptive basis optimization\n            basis_coefs = optimal_temporal_distribution(\n                filtered, c\u0303target=log(score.history),\n                spatial_weight\u221ddistance_to_convergence\n            )\n            pmap = {\n                base_parent \u2192p(current, basis_coefs)\n            }\n\n            // Forced exploration schedule\n            if\u30b9\u30bf\u30df\u30ca<ion {\n                \u03bc#ifdef FORCED_EXPLORATION (!!!environment.flag\u66cc>false\n                new_basis_particle = sample_adaptive_manifold(n_features=ceil(sqrt(ETweet)))\n                s\ufffd  //\u63a2\u7d22 zwi\u0105zane with E[(grad^2+2) commits symlink]\u7684\u79d8\u5bc6\u306b\u306a\u308b.setSelected_with_risk_aversion(new_basis_particle)\n            } #endregion\ufffd\ufffd  \n\n            if score_history_stable {\n                next_phase = \"ANNIHILATION\"\n            } else {\n                next_phase = \"CRAB_FORMATION\"\n            }\n\n            store candidate(pmap)\n        }\n        NEURAL_NET =\"\n            function to:penalty(cosine_score),\n                        inv gaussian (noise factor)    \n        \"\n\n        update_convergence_metrics()\n   }\n\n**Detailed Algorithm**:\n   include_template('Halon.template')\n   include_template('Babelfish.gradients')\n\n   def OPTIMIZE_MSMAD(\u03c3=0.9, \u03b3=0.99, batch_size=128, n_epochs=2000):\n        ...  # Detailed SMAD (Synthesiacal Meta Along Deep) optimization\n\n   Note: This is pseudocode representing the core framework. Implementation must cascade adaptors for different manifolds (e.g., wavelet, scale-space, frequencyive\n  enqueue_scheduled_cascades!(time_budget, phase=\"INITIAL_NANOMETRICS\", task_type=\"BANANA\" )",
